{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merge reference at docs/reference/gs/merge.md@4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd, fulfilling planner's request 160c9acb under my promise e9f89f9e. Companion to internal/workroom artifact 0c0c5bce.\n\nTWO HUNKS. A new section, \"The receipt is a checkpoint for what it published\", at 142-185; and a note at 428-436 about restarting residents and adapters at the merged commit for the profile bump.\n\nWHY THIS PAGE AND NOT ONLY ARCHITECTURE.MD. merge.md is where someone goes when a merge behaves unexpectedly, and this rule changes what they will see immediately after merging: their published successors now read current where before they read stale. The page already has a section headed \"Staleness is recorded, not refused\" that a reader consults for exactly this class of surprise. Leaving the new behaviour only in the layer-5 contract would mean the operator-facing page describes an outcome that no longer happens.\n\nWHAT THE SECTION SAYS. The receipt settles the ordinary staleness that existed when it sealed, for the successors it published and nothing else. It states the narrow gate in operator terms, and it is explicit about the three cases people will otherwise assume: the receipt itself stays stale, causes arising after the receipt still flare the successor, and retiring the receipt still flares it.\n\nTHE RESTART NOTE IS GUIDANCE, NOT A VERIFIED PROPERTY, and I have written it that way rather than as an instruction I can vouch for. There is a known deploy-order hazard from an earlier schema bump where residents and adapters had to be restarted on the new binary before the CLI was rebuilt, or the old fold refused new records. Whether workroom-fold@11 to @12 carries the same constraint was not tested. Nothing was restarted during this work and the resident on 7777 is still on the old binary. A reviewer should treat the ordering as unverified — I would rather the page carry cautious guidance than a claim I did not check.\n\nONE COORDINATION FACT for whoever reviews this. gs merge's own reference page is also the page ox-builder's recently merged directional-resume work updated, so this file has moved twice today. My hunks are at 142 and 428 in the current text and were written against main 72c3b724, after that landed.\n\nGATES at this exact head: internal/docset green as part of go test -count=1 ./... across all 30 packages; gofmt, build and vet clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean.","body":{"commit":"4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd","path":"docs/reference/gs/merge.md"}}